        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Is this expected, or should it happen only once?\n\nIt should happen only once and it does happen for me. After a fresh install adding `'javascript'` and `'typescript'` below [this line](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/70ade6783c9d45d5c81eab5a2d3ff3a62e02066e/configs/nvim-0.12/plugin/40_plugins.lua#L57), restarting to actually install new parsers, and then restarting again doesn't show any messages.\n\nThe problem is most likely with how Neovim installation is done installation, as it [checks if the previously installed parser is in the runtime](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/70ade6783c9d45d5c81eab5a2d3ff3a62e02066e/configs/nvim-0.12/plugin/40_plugins.lua#L64-L66). Probably some runtime issues, similar in how [described here](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/issues/35#issuecomment-3951658178). I'd suggest trying to download the [Nightly release](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/releases/tag/nightly) and test with it.",
