        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) after installing `tree-sitter-cli` via homebrew on MacOSX, the issue disappeared. I guess compiling the parsers failed silently on my system when starting neovim, therefore it was never saved.\n\nAh, makes sense. I wonder if this is an intended behavior of 'nvim-treesitter' to fail silently here or was it due to some other issues (like 'mini.starter' overriding the shown the message). I'll take a look.\n\nBut yeah, `:checkhealth vim.treesitter nvim-treesitter` (as a documented way to troubleshoot problems with tree-sitter) would have shown this issue.",
