        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "In init.lua, `vim.pack.add` is called to add `mini.nvim` plugin:\n\n```\nvim.pack.add({ Config.gh 'nvim-mini/mini.nvim' })\n```\n\nThis cannot be added so early because any PackChanged or PackChangedPre hooks will not be executed when the actual event occurs\n\nThe structure of the code need to changed to support vim.pack.add .  I propose:\n\ninit.lua - define only helper functions\nplugin/01_hooks.lua - code to add PackChanged and PackChangedPre hooks \nplugin/02_miniinit.lua - code to add mini.nvim and define helper functions that depend on mini.nvim \nplugin/* - the other files currently implemented\n\nReference: https://neovim.io/doc/user/pack/#PackChanged - scroll into end of example, it says:\n\n```\n-- If hooks need to run on install, run this before `vim.pack.add()`\n\n-- To act on install from lockfile, run before very first `vim.pack.add()`\n\n```\n",
            "created_at": "2026-06-01T04:20:07Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/issues/35#issuecomment-4589519950",
            "id": 4589519950,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/MiniMax/issues/35",
            "minimized": null,
