        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This cannot be added so early because any PackChanged or PackChangedPre hooks will not be executed when the actual event occurs\n\nAll events will be triggered during installation, no matter where the first `vim.pack.add()` is called. The MiniMax config doesn't define any installation hooks, and only they matter when installing from the lockfile. If users need installation hooks to act during lockfile, they need to be defined before the first `vim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim' })` call in 'init.lua'.\n\n> init.lua - define only helper functions\n\nThe problem is that those helper functions are useful almost immediately *and* they rely on 'mini.misc'. So 'mini.nvim' has to be installed very soon.\n\nI think moving `Config.on_packchanged` before 'mini.nvim' `vim.pack.add` might be reasonable here, though.",
            "created_at": "2026-06-01T09:21:23Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/issues/35#issuecomment-4591218137",
